1
00:00:00,770 --> 00:00:06,810
It's perfectly fine to get too into something or to laugh like an idiot.

2
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:10,740
And if anyone says otherwise, I'll beat them up!

3
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,200
Oh... she's right...

4
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:19,290
All I wanted...

5
00:00:20,790 --> 00:00:24,750
...was to be able to live and laugh freely.

6
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:28,250
Someone to tell me it was okay...

7
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:31,510
...to have meaning in my life.

8
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:38,180
The world has fallen in love

9
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:41,850
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

10
00:00:41,850 --> 00:00:45,140
I just want to understand you

11
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:49,520
Won't you open up to me?

12
00:00:56,450 --> 00:01:00,660
A fumbled exchange of words leaves a little taste of regret

13
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:04,000
Enough to make me cry

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,340
I want to link my racing emotions to the beat of my heart

15
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:16,470
and put it all in tune

16
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:22,310
I lost sight of everything but my goal

17
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:25,980
and had something important fade away

18
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:32,230
Let's start all over

19
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:37,360
The world has fallen in love

20
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:40,620
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

21
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:44,200
I want to know everything about you

22
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:48,370
Won't you tell me more?

23
00:01:48,370 --> 00:01:52,000
One inch feels like a million miles

24
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,920
as the days just seem to race by

25
00:01:55,590 --> 00:01:59,340
I won't and can't ever forget

26
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:02,600
this brightest page of my life.

27
00:02:14,690 --> 00:02:18,910
This is the first time I've seen Kou so vulnerable.

28
00:02:20,410 --> 00:02:26,410
He's counting on me to support him.

29
00:02:31,170 --> 00:02:33,840
He's pretty cute when he's like this.

30
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:37,800
This is my favorite scent.

31
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:40,930
Kou...

32
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:42,640
Not yet.

33
00:02:47,270 --> 00:02:48,770
Don't let go.

34
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,650
Huh? Why?

35
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:04,450
Oh... he doesn't want me to see him cry.

36
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:09,910
That must've been why he put his arms around me in the first place.

37
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:13,670
Sorry, I'm fine now.

38
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:16,250
Okay.

39
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:28,350
Oh no.

40
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:34,810
Half of me wants to support him in any way I can,

41
00:03:34,810 --> 00:03:41,360
but the other half just wants
to look at his tear-stained face.

42
00:03:43,610 --> 00:03:45,200
Hey, you know...

43
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:48,290
You make one heck of a face when you run.

44
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:52,460
You're so mean! How could you make fun of me when I was so desperately...

45
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:57,000
I'm not making fun of you.

46
00:03:59,090 --> 00:04:02,010
You were actually kind of cool.

47
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:05,800
By the light of the moon,

48
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:09,680
Kou's eyelashes glimmered.

49
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:14,190
His face had been stained with tears.

50
00:04:15,020 --> 00:04:16,940
I must be the only one

51
00:04:18,070 --> 00:04:20,150
to have ever seen him like this.

52
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:22,740
The only one he'd show this to.

53
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:31,580
Wait... isn't this the perfect time to confess?

54
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:23,920
Kou—

55
00:05:27,050 --> 00:05:27,760
grumble

56
00:05:29,010 --> 00:05:31,180
grumble

57
00:05:32,890 --> 00:05:34,810
Let's grab a bite and go home.

58
00:05:36,020 --> 00:05:40,230
Just like a couple! I feel bad for Yuuri, but I can't let this slip!

59
00:05:41,980 --> 00:05:43,780
Oh, we can't.

60
00:05:45,530 --> 00:05:50,660
I stopped by your house before I came, and Tanaka-sensei was there.

61
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:55,450
He probably made dinner and is waiting for you.

62
00:06:01,170 --> 00:06:04,090
Tanaka-sensei said something to me.

63
00:06:04,090 --> 00:06:07,840
He thought you bore a grudge against him.

64
00:06:10,050 --> 00:06:14,970
It's because he wasn't able to be by your side when you needed him the most.

65
00:06:14,970 --> 00:06:20,560
Huh? We were living so far apart that it's not like there was anything he could've done.

66
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:24,530
Yeah.

67
00:06:26,490 --> 00:06:30,990
I think you should tell him that yourself.

68
00:06:43,540 --> 00:06:44,500
Bye.

69
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:46,170
Oh, yeah.

70
00:06:47,010 --> 00:06:47,920
Bye.

71
00:06:50,970 --> 00:06:53,350
See you tomorrow!

72
00:06:52,970 --> 00:06:58,810
Before I knew it, I had run

73
00:06:52,970 --> 00:06:58,810
kudarizaka fumikiri made

74
00:06:54,970 --> 00:06:57,430
Yeah, see you at school.

75
00:06:57,430 --> 00:06:59,850
Yep, see you!

76
00:06:58,810 --> 00:07:03,810
all the way down to the train tracks.

77
00:06:58,810 --> 00:07:03,810
atashi wa muchuu de hashitta

78
00:07:03,810 --> 00:07:09,490
What I found was a train departing,

79
00:07:03,810 --> 00:07:09,490
kono koi wo saegiru you ni

80
00:07:04,230 --> 00:07:05,400
Yoshioka!

81
00:07:09,490 --> 00:07:14,370
densha wa sugisatta

82
00:07:09,490 --> 00:07:14,370
taking my love with it.

83
00:07:11,450 --> 00:07:12,530
Thanks.

84
00:07:14,370 --> 00:07:20,040
Distant memories, shining seas.

85
00:07:14,370 --> 00:07:20,040
tooi hi no kioku umi no kagayaki

86
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:16,490
Yeah!

87
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:22,920
Seasons pass.

88
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:22,920
kisetsu wa meguru

89
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:27,300
Now, I squint up at the clouds.

90
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:27,300
hikoukigumo ni me wo hosomete

91
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:32,680
A sunflower swayed in the breeze,

92
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:32,680
chiisaku yureta himawari

93
00:07:30,550 --> 00:07:32,260
It opened.

94
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:39,060
sayonara mo ienai mata

95
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:39,060
seeing how I couldn't even say goodbye.

96
00:07:33,550 --> 00:07:36,760
Kou's door really opened.

97
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:40,310
You've finally stepped outside, right?

98
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:48,900
We were so tantalizingly close, yet so far apart.

99
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:48,900
hon no suumiri no sukima de sotto kusuguru itami

100
00:07:41,190 --> 00:07:44,610
But even if you won't come out this time,

101
00:07:46,070 --> 00:07:49,240
I'll just kick that door down again.

102
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:54,450
If only the summer fireworks

103
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:54,450
manatsu ni kieta hanabi ga

104
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:54,160
I'll kick it down any time you need me!

105
00:07:54,450 --> 00:08:00,370
had appeared before my tears...

106
00:07:54,450 --> 00:08:00,370
namida no saki ni utsureba

107
00:08:00,370 --> 00:08:05,790
I will definitely remember.

108
00:08:00,370 --> 00:08:05,790
I will kitto omoidasu wa

109
00:08:05,790 --> 00:08:17,560
Please know that I'll be here, waiting for you.

110
00:08:05,790 --> 00:08:17,560
anata ni todoke kono basho de atashi wa matteiru

111
00:08:08,090 --> 00:08:11,010
You desperately keep running to save me

112
00:08:11,010 --> 00:08:14,430
no matter how many times you fail.

113
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:39,290
Mabuchi

114
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:39,290
Tanaka

115
00:08:39,290 --> 00:08:42,120
Hey, you're back!

116
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:44,540
Yeah...

117
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:50,170
What about dinner?

118
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:52,130
Sure...

119
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:07,520
Hey, Dad. Welcome home.

120
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:09,230
Is that you, Youichi?

121
00:09:09,690 --> 00:09:11,780
Came over again, did you?

122
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:22,370
Just a minute, Dad. I'm almost done...

123
00:09:24,790 --> 00:09:29,290
Man, I'm starving. Guess I'll eat tonight.

124
00:09:31,710 --> 00:09:35,220
Great! Kou, can you serve the rice?

125
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:40,300
Don't forget to get chopsticks for everyone.

126
00:09:40,890 --> 00:09:41,810
Sure.

127
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,450
Welcome back.

128
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,410
I see.

129
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,210
Thanks.

130
00:10:22,050 --> 00:10:23,850
All right, help yourselves.

131
00:10:24,390 --> 00:10:25,770
Thanks for the food.

132
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:27,560
Thanks for the food.

133
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:27,560
Thanks for the food.

134
00:10:37,950 --> 00:10:42,700
You know, I've waited so long for this day.

135
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:50,290
I wanted to keep smiling all the way through.

136
00:10:51,830 --> 00:10:53,710
Guess I couldn't keep it up.

137
00:10:57,460 --> 00:11:00,800
After Mom died, I didn't know

138
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:03,550
whether coming back to this house alone

139
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:06,520
and eating together like this without her

140
00:11:07,270 --> 00:11:08,600
was really okay.

141
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:15,570
I didn't know if it was okay to do all the things Mom wasn't able to.

142
00:11:16,570 --> 00:11:17,610
I never knew...

143
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,700
Kou...

144
00:11:22,950 --> 00:11:25,200
Your mother...

145
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:32,750
She wasn't that uncaring a woman.

146
00:11:40,470 --> 00:11:42,010
Kou 6 y.o.

147
00:11:40,470 --> 00:11:42,010
Kou 7 y.o.

148
00:11:40,470 --> 00:11:42,010
Kou 8 y.o.

149
00:11:40,470 --> 00:11:42,010
Youichi 5 y.o.

150
00:11:40,470 --> 00:11:42,010
Youichi 6 y.o.

151
00:11:40,470 --> 00:11:42,010
Youichi 7 y.o.

152
00:11:40,470 --> 00:11:43,510
Youichi 8 y.o.

153
00:12:06,370 --> 00:12:11,000
Yeah. Tonight's dinner is delicious.

154
00:12:12,710 --> 00:12:14,210
It really is.

155
00:12:17,590 --> 00:12:19,130
We have plenty to go around.

156
00:12:19,130 --> 00:12:22,090
You eat too, Kou. It's delicious.

157
00:12:25,430 --> 00:12:27,260
About my family name...

158
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:33,390
Could I wait a while longer to change it back?

159
00:12:34,690 --> 00:12:38,360
It's not that I'm against being called Tanaka again.

160
00:12:39,610 --> 00:12:40,530
It's just...

161
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:46,700
Changing your name in high school
could cause quite a stir.

162
00:12:48,870 --> 00:12:51,450
All right, I understand.

163
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:55,960
We can wait until after you sort your feelings.

164
00:12:57,330 --> 00:13:02,170
Even if our names are different, we'll always be a family.

165
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:07,970
Mabuchi

166
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:07,970
Tanaka

167
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:07,260
Thanks, Dad.

168
00:13:16,230 --> 00:13:19,020
I guess Kou's not here yet.

169
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:25,280
I got a little carried away last night and ended up doing some crazy things,

170
00:13:26,530 --> 00:13:30,990
but now that I have a chance to breathe, the embarrassment is catching up.

171
00:13:32,490 --> 00:13:35,580
Even if we consider what happened just a friend helping a friend,

172
00:13:36,330 --> 00:13:39,290
that doesn't mean it'll be any
less awkward to face him today.

173
00:13:40,040 --> 00:13:41,250
What about Kou?

174
00:13:42,170 --> 00:13:45,420
How's he going to handle it?

175
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,270
M-Morning...

176
00:13:57,810 --> 00:14:01,820
Looks like he's just as flustered as me.

177
00:14:04,110 --> 00:14:06,070
I guess that makes sense.

178
00:14:20,790 --> 00:14:23,840
What did he just do? It was so adorable!

179
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:26,130
Did Kou always act like that?

180
00:14:27,050 --> 00:14:29,180
Crap, I can't keep a straight face.

181
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:33,890
Where were you yesterday?!

182
00:14:35,180 --> 00:14:38,190
I can't believe you ditched us.

183
00:14:38,190 --> 00:14:41,400
Yeah, me neither. Sorry about that.

184
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:43,690
You sure don't sound like you're sorry.

185
00:14:44,780 --> 00:14:46,900
How about today? Are you free?

186
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:50,780
What did you just say?

187
00:14:50,780 --> 00:14:54,660
I'll do as much as I can. How's that sound?

188
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:57,960
Really? I'm free all day.

189
00:14:57,960 --> 00:15:01,250
Damn, I'm think I'm gonna cry... just kidding.

190
00:15:01,250 --> 00:15:02,960
Let's do it!

191
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:04,250
Sounds good to me.

192
00:15:05,050 --> 00:15:05,840
Okay.

193
00:15:06,210 --> 00:15:10,510
You can count on us to keep
those summer lessons at bay!

194
00:15:11,510 --> 00:15:13,970
Leave it all to us!

195
00:15:42,330 --> 00:15:44,170
What the heck is this?

196
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:47,590
Just my way of saying thanks.

197
00:15:48,130 --> 00:15:49,920
Sorry, I guess.

198
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:54,390
You all went out of your way to help me study,
and I outscored every one of you.

199
00:15:51,340 --> 00:15:55,390
Mabuchi
Kou

200
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:58,350
You're pretty spiteful, aren't you?

201
00:15:58,350 --> 00:16:01,440
Man, I was not expecting this.

202
00:16:02,850 --> 00:16:07,650
I'm so glad we all got into the top section!
It's my first time ever!

203
00:16:07,650 --> 00:16:09,940
We didn't put in all that effort for nothing.

204
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:11,200
You're right.

205
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:17,120
You can say that again. Now we can focus on making vacation plans.

206
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:21,290
That's right! Nothing but good times ahead of us!

207
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:23,580
I always get shaky knees up here.

208
00:16:25,580 --> 00:16:27,000
You're right there, Touma.

209
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,420
Huh, seriously?

210
00:16:29,630 --> 00:16:30,800
Wow, I am!

211
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:34,380
It's the guy from the library!

212
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:38,600
The molester!

213
00:16:39,430 --> 00:16:40,600
Wait, Touma?

214
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:43,560
Hey, wasn't he—

215
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:45,850
Not a word! I'm ashamed!

216
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:51,900
A-Anyway, let the good times begin! It's summer!

217
00:16:52,530 --> 00:16:54,860
Summer is here!

218
00:16:59,950 --> 00:17:04,540
I know you're excited for summer vacation,
but don't get yourselves into too much trouble.

219
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:05,920
You're dismissed.

220
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:10,710
Hey, are you free now?

221
00:17:10,710 --> 00:17:12,460
Sure, let's hang out somewhere.

222
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:14,800
We need to sort out our plans, anyway.

223
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:15,970
Sounds good to me.

224
00:17:15,970 --> 00:17:17,340
Kou, what about...

225
00:17:18,550 --> 00:17:20,510
Wait, where'd he go?

226
00:17:20,510 --> 00:17:23,270
I just saw him leaving with his bag.

227
00:17:23,270 --> 00:17:23,980
He's so quick!

228
00:17:25,730 --> 00:17:27,060
And Kominato-kun is...

229
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:28,650
And the AC was broken!

230
00:17:28,650 --> 00:17:31,360
Looks like he's busy.

231
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:33,780
Alright, then let's go after Kou!

232
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:35,780
Wait up, Futaba-chan!

233
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:38,320
He probably hasn't left the building yet.

234
00:17:42,910 --> 00:17:44,620
Shuuko!

235
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:45,790
Shuu-chan!

236
00:17:46,210 --> 00:17:48,670
You two can go get Mabuchi.

237
00:17:48,670 --> 00:17:50,420
Got it!

238
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:52,960
We'll wait for you at the entrance!

239
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,720
They sure are lively.

240
00:18:02,510 --> 00:18:04,770
Shuuko! Shuu-chan!

241
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:10,940
Futaba-chan.

242
00:18:10,940 --> 00:18:13,650
I'm gonna get serious this summer!

243
00:18:16,950 --> 00:18:18,530
M-Me too!

244
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,370
Okay!

245
00:18:26,910 --> 00:18:27,660
There he is!

246
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:28,420
Kou!

247
00:18:30,250 --> 00:18:31,960
Gotcha!

248
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:33,050
What?

249
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:40,340
I think that's the first time I've heard someone

250
00:18:41,510 --> 00:18:43,180
call you by your first name.

251
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:45,020
I'm glad.

252
00:18:46,730 --> 00:18:48,940
Just because I found a place to belong

253
00:18:50,150 --> 00:18:53,770
doesn't mean that my feelings have changed.

254
00:18:54,610 --> 00:19:00,530
I bet you thought you were done with having to put up with me.

255
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:06,790
And what if I told you that I've never thought of it as "putting up with you"?

256
00:19:09,210 --> 00:19:11,670
He's not fair. I let down my guard.

257
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:15,460
Happy summer vacation.

258
00:19:18,510 --> 00:19:20,970
Holiday greetings already?

259
00:19:24,350 --> 00:19:28,890
If you're going to lead Murao on
just to hurt her in the end,

260
00:19:29,890 --> 00:19:32,230
I won't let you go unpunished.

261
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:35,650
Is that all?

262
00:19:37,150 --> 00:19:41,030
So it's okay as long as I don't
end up hurting her, right?

263
00:19:44,370 --> 00:19:46,120
Happy summer vacation.

264
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:51,330
In a town beset by a sudden shower,

265
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:50,830
He pisses me off!

266
00:19:51,250 --> 00:19:54,790
I like Kou, but his brother sucks!

267
00:19:51,330 --> 00:19:56,710
I say "See you later", and wave goodbye.

268
00:19:56,040 --> 00:19:57,750
Kominato-kun!

269
00:19:56,710 --> 00:20:02,180
As I watch you pass through the ticket gate, I think:

270
00:19:58,090 --> 00:20:00,970
Hey, what're you all doing here?

271
00:20:01,430 --> 00:20:04,890
We're gonna hang out somewhere and talk about what to do over break.

272
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:07,470
"It never goes according to plan, does it?"

273
00:20:04,890 --> 00:20:07,720
That sounds like a plan. Let's do it!

274
00:20:07,470 --> 00:20:17,190
Everything seemed incredibly fragile that day,

275
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:11,770
Seriously, couldn't we just
set everything up over text?

276
00:20:11,770 --> 00:20:13,230
What are you saying?

277
00:20:13,810 --> 00:20:16,980
It's way more fun to decide these things when we're all together!

278
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:19,860
Yeah, she's spot on, Kou.

279
00:20:17,190 --> 00:20:22,780
but it passed, as days tend to do.

280
00:20:20,690 --> 00:20:22,280
Be a man and come.

281
00:20:22,650 --> 00:20:23,950
Okay?

282
00:20:23,950 --> 00:20:25,990
So, you wanna do this at Nuts Donuts?

283
00:20:23,950 --> 00:20:33,330
The rails carry you away

284
00:20:26,990 --> 00:20:29,700
Guess I'm stuck with them for the long haul.

285
00:20:30,330 --> 00:20:31,250
Kou!

286
00:20:32,830 --> 00:20:33,830
Let's go.

287
00:20:33,330 --> 00:20:41,590
leaving me alone on our usual path.

288
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:52,230
The words I prepared for you are so simple,

289
00:20:51,770 --> 00:20:53,600
At first, I was alone.

290
00:20:52,230 --> 00:21:00,940
so why can't I say them?

291
00:20:56,310 --> 00:20:57,520
But...

292
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:03,820
I wanted to change.

293
00:21:02,690 --> 00:21:07,910
Why can't I?

294
00:21:05,070 --> 00:21:06,990
I decided to change.

295
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:20,000
"Even when communication breaks down

296
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:25,930
we can always just start over

297
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:27,590
And now, I think I've done it.

298
00:21:25,930 --> 00:21:31,060
and go back to step one,"

299
00:21:29,180 --> 00:21:33,520
I did it by sharing this time with my friends.

300
00:21:31,060 --> 00:21:36,690
come the words out of my mouth to reassure you.

301
00:21:47,820 --> 00:21:53,250
Time is running out for me to find the right words—

302
00:21:53,250 --> 00:21:58,710
the train is nearing the crossroads.

303
00:21:58,710 --> 00:22:04,210
How will things between us turn out

304
00:22:04,210 --> 00:22:15,640
once I show you everything inside my aching heart?

305
00:22:19,980 --> 00:22:28,990
My heart is dumb, but not weak.

306
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:24,730
It's still too early to reminisce.

307
00:22:25,990 --> 00:22:29,530
We've only just started.

308
00:22:29,410 --> 00:22:38,040
We couldn't get it right today, either.

309
00:22:30,780 --> 00:22:34,580
There are still countless memories to be made.

310
00:22:38,830 --> 00:22:48,300
The rails carry you away

311
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:56,640
leaving me alone on our usual path.

312
00:22:57,680 --> 00:23:07,150
The words I prepared for you are so simple,

313
00:23:02,610 --> 00:23:06,570
From now on out, we'll hold our heads high

314
00:23:06,570 --> 00:23:08,740
and walk forward, one step at a time.

315
00:23:07,150 --> 00:23:15,410
so why can't I say them?

316
00:23:10,450 --> 00:23:13,740
Youth. A blue spring.

317
00:23:16,410 --> 00:23:22,420
We'll ride forward, on the stormy wind coursing through our hearts.

318
00:23:17,700 --> 00:23:22,880
Why can't I?
